config DRM_APPLE_ADBE
	tristate "DRM support for the Apple A9 display pipe"
	depends on DRM && OF && ARM64 && MMU
	depends on ARCH_APPLE || COMPILE_TEST
	select APERTURE_HELPERS
	select DRM_CLIENT_SELECTION
	select DRM_GEM_DMA_HELPER
	select DRM_KMS_HELPER
	help
	  KMS driver for the A9 (S8000/S8003) disp0 pipe that iBoot leaves
	  running. It adopts the boot mode, takes the framebuffer over from
	  simpledrm, and adds page flips through the pipe's parameter FIFO
	  and vblank interrupts. It never programs timings, clocks, power or
	  the eDP link. Scanout buffers are DMA (CMA) allocations.

	  Built in, it replaces simpledrm during boot. Booting with
	  apple_adbe_drm.enable=0 keeps simpledrm instead.

	  If M is selected, the module is called apple_adbe_drm.

config APPLE_ADBE_PROBE
	tristate "Apple A9 display pipe probe and FIFO measurements"
	depends on ARM64 && OF && DEBUG_FS
	help
	  Observe the A9 iBoot display without taking over simpledrm. By
	  default the probe only reads registers and polls the frame counter.
	  Module parameters opt into one bounded IRQ test, a read-only DART
	  snapshot, a parameter FIFO re-send of the live plane, or one
	  auto-reverting flip to a second buffer. No link training, power
	  management or IOMMU programming is done.

	  If unsure, say N. The module is called apple_adbe_probe.
